  "behavior": [
    "Two-party ownership offer/accept/cancel/decline for an existing member, with exact durable originals and separate queued/uncertain/accepted/rejected state.",
    "Private-channel handover waits for the accepting client current scope/epoch/bindings before a distinct completion. Temporary preparation grants reading, not new staff or writing rights.",
    "Signed admissions commit bounded exact encrypted history originals before transport, so losing the admission reply cannot strand history after role/key rotation. Delivery still requires the intended currently authorized nonretired recipient.",
    "Departure ends an offer; cancellation retires temporary access. Actual removal changes future MLS keys while prior received copies remain readable. Former owner becomes ordinary member without residual staff powers.",
    "Capability-gated native offer/accept/decline/cancel controls disclose responsibility and private access. Stale accepting dialogs dismiss and disable after another device accepts.",
    "Compact channel-access confirmation has a scrollable complete explanation. Named captures wait for intended native and Compose states within original interaction bounds; fresh rendered proof remains required."
  ],
  "protocolBoundary": "Initial functional Spaces v1 remains unreleased and undeployed. Exact public beta90b5aadb has no core SpaceClient. Manifests apply to all new admissions, including those preceding an ownership offer. Absent-manifest pending originals retain their old post-ack recovery path. No mixed pre-release reader compatibility is claimed.",
